# BSan gate of libavutil/formats wave 0 at 7317de905c — FAILED (equiv binary only)

Gate: clippy, plain, asan-ubsan, tsan, bsan lib/ub_safe/ub_unsafe all pass; `bsan` equiv fails.
Command: BSAN_OPTIONS=gc_hang_threshold_ms=600000 CRUSTIFY_FFMPEG_VARIANT=bsan cargo bsan test --test equiv -- --skip compile_fail

Orchestrator triage (same binary, BSAN_SYMBOLIZER set):
- reproduces on a second full multi-threaded run;
- passes with --test-threads=1 (348/348);
- passes for the new formats modules alone (channel_layout pixfmt pixdesc samplefmt imgutils csp pixelutils)
  and for every old module with those skipped;
- module pairs: `cpu:: imgutils::` FAILS; every other pair of {cpu, opt, log} x {new modules} passes;
- `cpu::` alone and `channel_layout::matrix_encoding::option_default_and_range_span_the_named_values` alone pass.
Report site: C av_strtod (libavutil/eval.c:120) reading `next`, reached from av_parse_cpu_caps ->
av_opt_eval_flags -> set_string_number, whose token lives in a C stack buffer. The new
tests/equiv/imgutils.rs `captured()` installs a process-wide Rust log callback (`log::set_callback::<Capture>`)
under LogState while the cpu tests (which do not take LogState) log from other threads.
Undecided: real race/UB in the log-callback wrapper or test harness, vs a BSan false positive
(cf. the dead-frame provenance note for stack-passed C pointers). Promotion is blocked until resolved.

